#!/bin/sh
# Name: Steb
# Author: hzwei.dev
# Icon: data:image/png;base64,
# DontUseFBInk

# The home-screen tile. Any .sh in documents/ is indexed as though it were a
# book, which is the whole reason this file exists — it puts Steb one tap away
# in the library. It is *only* a door: everything real lives in the extension at
# /mnt/us/extensions/steb, and both this tile and the KUAL entry run the same
# bin/steb.sh wrapper, so the launch logging and the download-directory check
# stay single-sourced.
#
# DontUseFBInk: the app owns the screen through its own X11 window, so the
# framework must not paint stdout/stderr underneath it.
#
# Only the `# Icon:` line above is generated — it is one ~21KB base64 data URI,
# so rerun device/make-tile.sh after changing assets/cover.svg. Everything else
# here is hand-edited.
#
# Deliberately no `# UseHooks`. The on_install hook would be a tidy place to
# create the download directory, but this plain-body form is the one proven on
# these devices, and bin/steb.sh already creates the directory on every launch —
# so hooks would buy nothing and risk the one file that has to work.

# Don't stack a second picker on a double tap: re-launching over a running one
# can leave the framework SIGSTOP'd and the screen frozen.
#
# This asks only whether the name `steb` is taken, so nothing else long-lived
# started from that binary may answer to it.
if pidof steb >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    exit 0
fi
nohup sh -c 'sleep 1; exec /mnt/us/extensions/steb/bin/steb.sh' >/dev/null 2>&1 &
